# Guild Points System — Overview

**Source of truth:** [especificacao-guild-points-rf-online.md](../../especificacao-guild-points-rf-online.md) — consult before implementing business logic or architecture.

## Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React + React Query + SCSS (`frontend/`) |
| Backend | Spring Boot + PostgreSQL (`backend/`) |
| Real-time | STOMP over SockJS |

Monorepo: `frontend/` and `backend/` at repo root. Do not edit the plan file.

## Roles (hierarchy)

`MEMBRO` < `MODERADOR` < `ADMINISTRADOR` = `LIDER` (single leader enforced in DB).

- **Backend must validate role** on every sensitive endpoint — never trust frontend-only checks.
- Mutations (Objetivo, Evento, Leilão, Item, point adjustments) require Líder/Administrador.
- Moderador+ approves registrations.

## Critical implementation rules

- **Atomic operations:** event claims and auction bids must be idempotent; use transactions with optimistic/pessimistic locks.
- **Audit everything:** point changes, profile edits, approvals, auctions → `AuditLogService`.
- **Real-time:** Events, auctions, logs, available balance via shared WebSocket client (frontend) / STOMP topics (backend).
- Prefer spec section numbers when tracing requirements (e.g. §9 Leilões, §8 Itens).
